# Response headers for Cloudflare Workers static assets (copied to dist/_headers by astro build). Cloudflare applies
# them to every response whose path matches, including the 404 page served for unknown paths (rule /*).
# Limits: 2,000 characters per line and 100 rules; the build fails past either (scripts/csp/csp.mts).
#
# X-Robots-Tag: noindex keeps search engines from indexing the workers.dev URL as a duplicate. Removed at the
# switch to the custom domain (plan.md Task 4.2). robots.txt must never Disallow, or crawlers can't see it.
#
# Content-Security-Policy: the line below is a fail-closed placeholder. After every astro build, the cspHeaders()
# integration (scripts/csp/csp.mts) hashes every inline <script> and <style> in dist/ and replaces it in
# dist/_headers with the real policy. Served unreplaced, it blocks everything, so a missed step can't ship a site
# without a CSP. Edit the policy in scripts/csp/csp.mts (buildPolicy), not here.
#
# Permissions-Policy denies features the site never uses. The clipboard stays allowed (the email Copy button).
# Only names current Chrome recognizes: an unknown one is a console error on every page (browsing-topics was dropped
# for that reason). tests/e2e/csp.spec.ts fails on any such header error.
# X-Frame-Options repeats frame-ancestors 'none' for browsers without CSP level 2. HSTS: no includeSubDomains or
# preload until the custom domain is decided (plan.md Task 4.2).
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), serial=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Opens in the browser; saving it uses the published file name. The "Download Resume" buttons use the
# <a download> attribute to download instead.
/resume.pdf
  Content-Disposition: inline; filename="Shahar_Asher_CV.pdf"
